    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Do you think learning English is difficult? There are about 6,500 languages in the world. Many people think that some languages are harder to learn than others. A European, for example, may find it more difficult to learn Japanese than English. Why is this so?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Linguists",
            "zh": "语言学家"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " study the history of the world’s languages. They have divided languages into “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "families",
            "zh": "语系"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "”. The languages have been put into a “tree”. The distance between two languages is called their “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "linguistic",
            "zh": "语言的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " distance”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "You can look up the “tree” for the foreign language you want to learn. How far is it from yours? The "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "farther",
            "ref": "v-farther"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it is, the harder it will likely be for you to learn this new language."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "For example, French, Spanish and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Hindi",
            "zh": "印地语"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " all belong to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Indo-European family",
            "zh": "印欧语系"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But French and Spanish are in one "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "subgroup",
            "zh": "亚群"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", while Hindi is in another. This means French is “closer” to Spanish than to Hindi. As a result, most French speakers will find it easier to learn Spanish than to learn Hindi."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Besides, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "effect",
            "ref": "v-effect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of this “distance” is "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mutual",
            "ref": "v-mutual"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". A Chinese person, for example, will face a certain level of difficulty when learning English. In the opposite direction, when a British person tries to learn Chinese, he or she will be faced with "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "similar",
            "ref": "v-similar"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " difficulties!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
